WEBVTT

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.770
You're all here.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.110
I'm your coach, Fudou.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.660
From here on out, you guys will be fighting Inazuma Japan.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.060
Inazuma Japan?

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.080
Why us?

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.080
It was requested by Coach Kuroiwa.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.020
Fight with Inazuma Japan.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.250
Okay.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.710
I'll give them proper training.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:30.760
No.

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:35.040
Training them is far too lenient. Destroy them.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.970
What do you mean, Kageyama-san?

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.680
I mean, Coach Kuroiwa.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.370
Crush them into dust.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.860
I don't care if it breaks them.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.750
Let's do it, Coach Fudou.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.180
He took it again!

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:41.550
Yes!

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.330
Your speed really is amazing.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.770
I'm gradually getting the idea of how much power I should put into it.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.640
I won't lose to anyone when it comes to running.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.520
So, after I get the ball, I'll send it to you.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.750
That's my role.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:57.360
Yeah!

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.370
Then let's keep this up and win the preliminary finals!

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:08.290
That's the sort of teammate you're looking for, isn't it? Captain.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.630
Everyone! Your opponent for the finals has been decided!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:16.080
Which is it, Uzbekistan or the UAE?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.380
It's Uzbekistan.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.880
Them, huh?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.010
Their team's name is Storm Wolf.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.090
Just one more match and we'll be representing Asia, huh?

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.950
You really can accomplish something once you put your mind to it.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:29.490
Honestly, I didn't expect that we'd accomplish this much.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.870
The finals, huh?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.190
I'd sure like to win!

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.060
Yeah, you're right.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.370
We'll continue.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.040
I don't get it.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.440
Why is Shindou always so hard on Ibuki?

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.470
You should be worrying more about yourself.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.730
Their captain Dmitri and Maxim are the key forwards.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:18.940
While these two keep the opponent team occupied, their third forward Zaul heads for the goal.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:24.360
Their midfielders are Loran and Aaron, with their playmaker Ruslan at the center.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.370
From the data alone, they give a very solid impression.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.710
Their defense is rather interesting.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.220
They pair up into twos and act as a wall to block off shoots.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.460
Because of that, the ball doesn't reach their goalkeeper.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.840
But there's one thing I've noticed.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.280
Their playmaker Ruslan?

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.130
It's not just him. The team's attitude overall is far too energetic.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.350
Meaning?

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.600
Until last year, Storm Wolf was well-known for their emotionless plays.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:05:02.420
Not even their captain Dmitri's face would change expression whenever he made a shoot.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.270
This tournament has been full of inconsistencies like that.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.870
Is that Uzbekistan's team?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.780
Yes.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:12.830
Want to watch with us?

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:14.620
No thanks.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.830
Doing the research is your job.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.550
So, have you found their weakness yet?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.420
You really get under my skin every time.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:26.040
Sorry.

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:27.890
I apologize if I touched a nerve.

00:05:35.070 --> 00:05:36.440
Matatagi-kun!

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.110
You're a very interesting person.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.440
Interesting? Me?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.200
I got a glimpse of the darkness that's inside of you the other day.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:49.730
<i>It's impossible for people to truly understand one another.</i>

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.530
<i>You would be better off just making yourself look like you're getting along with them.</i>

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.830
I've been wondering about you ever since.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.350
It was very surprising.

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.290
A bit hard to imagine those words coming from you, considering how you act normally.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.300
So? What are you going to do about it?

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.010
Is that the real you?

00:06:07.530 --> 00:06:09.890
What do you mean, the real me?

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:11.970
Is something wrong?

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.730
Nothing.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.810
Well, I've got practice.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.310
The depths of Matatagi-kun's character seem bottomless.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:24.440
Observing him will be most interesting.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.160
I'm feeling a good response from them.

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:31.950
You mean the team?

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:32.710
Yeah.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.120
I was really worried about how we'd do at first.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:38.820
But I kept telling myself anyway that things will work out somehow,

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:42.550
and I was anxious about having to pull everyone along as Captain.

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:44.040
I know.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.710
I knew that.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:51.530
But seeing you worry over that made me think that you were the most reliable person for the job.

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:53.180
Huh? Really?

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:57.440
Even though you worry, you've always managed to find the answer.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:02.240
I think that cycle is how Matsukaze Tenma was able to grow stronger as a captain.

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:05.070
I see.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.900
What are you two talking about?

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.480
Sorry, didn't mean to surprise you.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.420
I was just telling Tenma that he's become a good captain!

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.150
H-Hey, Aoi!

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.240
She's right!

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.930
This team wouldn't get anywhere without Captain.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.750
Not you too, Matatagi!

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.710
Come on, let's go practice!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:22.250
All right!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.970
I really think we can win the finals.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:29.670
They all have such good expressions.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.760
Good expressions?

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:33.820
Yeah.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.890
Wouldn't you agree, Mizukawa-san?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.620
They don't look all that different to me.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.270
Everyone, gather up!

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:48.350
You will be having a practice match tomorrow.

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.310
A practice match?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:51.860
At this point in time?

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:54.570
Which team is it?

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.200
You will know when you meet them.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:12.670
I'm getting pretty good, right?

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:14.640
Yeah.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:19.020
How do I say it? It's like, this is starting to get really fun.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:23.100
And it feels great to win.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:29.860
The way it's gotten now though, I'm finding just how difficult this is to master.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:31.110
I see.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:35.320
I wish I can reach your level soon.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:42.290
Maybe soccer works for me better than I thought.

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:47.250
After all, I don't have to use my hands.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.470
Be careful, Tetsukado.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:52.820
What?

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.730
Soccer is fun...

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:59.680
...but if you get impatient about climbing to the top, you'll find yourself being almost flattened by walls everywhere you go.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.580
It's dangerous to push yourself.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.140
Are you speaking from experience?

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.650
Yeah.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.040
But now you're here, so you've managed to conquer that, right?

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.150
I have a friend who was once my enemy.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:17.310
It was thanks to him that I was able to overcome my walls.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:19.680
A friend who was your enemy, huh...

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:21.750
Are you still connected to him now?

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:22.860
Yeah.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:25.620
It's a bond that can't be broken even if either of us tried.

00:09:27.930 --> 00:09:29.420
This is going to be fun!

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:32.090
We've improved so much since we started!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.910
Yeah.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:38.510
I'm sure it'll be a good match, even in terms of testing our abilities!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:41.260
We might even create new hissatsu techniques.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:47.840
Practicing with an opponent rather than amongst ourselves will also help us to overcome any challenges.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:52.320
Practice is no excuse. I won't let them earn a single point.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:54.650
Naturally.

00:10:03.640 --> 00:10:04.120
That's...

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:16.860
Hakuryuu!

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:17.930
It's not just him.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:19.930
They're all...

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:23.450
You will be playing against them.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.770
These guys are Resistance Japan.

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:32.270
And I'm the coach, Fudou!

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.110
Resistance Japan?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.280
It's been a while, Tsurugi.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:41.450
I wasn't expecting to face off with you again in this way.

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.660
Is he the friend who used to be an enemy?

00:10:45.980 --> 00:10:49.160
We've come here today to crush you.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:50.620
Crush us?

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:55.480
Let's take this time to introduce the members of my Resistance Japan.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.720
I am Hakuryuu, from Team Zero of the former Fifth Sector.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.760
Minamisawa Atsushi.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:05.600
Gassan Kunimitsu Jr. High.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:07.350
Yukimura Hyouga.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:09.690
Hakuren Jr. High.

00:11:10.510 --> 00:11:11.770
Namikawa Rensuke.

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:14.260
Kaiou Academy.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.860
Give us everything you've got today, you scalywags!

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:18.900
Kurosaki Makoto.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.360
Seidouzan Jr. High.

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:23.150
Makari Ginjirou.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.490
Hakuren Jr. High.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.040
Kita Ichiban.

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.500
Tengawara Jr. High.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.500
Mahoro Tadashi.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.500
Gen'ei Academy.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:35.380
Kishibe Taiga.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.130
Kidokawa Seishuu Jr. High.

00:11:38.820 --> 00:11:40.010
Gomaki Tetsurou.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.130
From Dragon Link.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:43.930
Senguuji Yamato.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:46.850
Also from Dragon Link.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:49.930
Those are my eleven.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.910
Their team is full of amazing members.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:56.840
Almost all of them are strikers.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:59.570
So they're a team with super offense.

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.570
Defending is going to be a tough task.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.280
Don't worry. I'll stop them.

00:12:04.670 --> 00:12:05.870
Just watch me.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.270
But they said they're going to crush us.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.330
Okay, everyone!

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.110
The world is almost within reach!

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:17.960
Let's win this and ride on the momentum!

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:22.020
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:25.390
We are...

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:28.750
New Inazuma Japan!

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:32.820
What lies ahead of the world is the introduction of New Inazuma Japan's Character posters!

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.770
Inazuma Eleven GO CharaPos collection 7! On sale soon!

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.570
It's finally here!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:41.350
Our CharaPos collection!

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:44.680
The best LBX players now in your home!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:45.970
This is so great!

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:47.700
All right! Begin War Time!

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:51.310
Danball Senki CharaPos collection! On sale soon!

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:56.820
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:13:00.540 --> 00:13:04.190
This is a friendly between Inazuma Japan and Resistance Japan!

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:07.260
I will act as referee.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.770
Begin the kickoff!

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:16.100
Here we go!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:21.570
Sakura!

00:13:21.920 --> 00:13:23.070
Okay!

00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.750
Is that all you've got?

00:13:26.750 --> 00:13:29.260
Don't look down on me because I'm a girl!

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.370
Sakura, don't push yourself!

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:33.120
I fix my own mistakes!

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.920
That guy is really annoying!

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:44.630
Here he comes!

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:51.990
White Hurricane!

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.770
Panther Blizzard!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:08.930
A shoot chain!

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.530
What incredible power!

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:25.590
That shoot was unbelievable...

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:28.530
Are you okay?

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:31.140
That was completely different from what I'd seen so far...

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:31.720
What?

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.180
Shindou and them have been fighting against guys like that...?

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.570
Do you see?

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.880
This is our difference in rank.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.110
Shindou-san.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:49.510
From the looks of that shoot chain, they really do mean to destroy us.

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:50.990
It's a challenge we'll have to accept.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:57.330
Let's do our best to bring out even more of everyone's abilities during this game!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.040
But be careful.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.460
That wasn't the fullest extent of their power.

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.460
Why did you arrange this match?

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:13.510
Because the team must be made aware of something before they play the finals.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:21.850
Hey, track team!

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:24.280
What the hell was up with that dribbling?

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.900
You looked like you were going in slow mo!

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:31.610
You...!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.080
Yukimura!

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.800
Damn it!

00:15:58.570 --> 00:15:59.510
Tetsukado!

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:01.390
Yeah, leave it to me!

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:05.900
Tetsukado!

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:07.420
What's the matter?

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.740
You can't win against us with your tail between your legs.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.520
We're not finished yet. You still have to learn your lesson!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.520
Mahoro!

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:24.120
Phantom Shot!

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:31.510
What?!

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:35.680
This doesn't make sense!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.970
We ought to be able to do more!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.930
I didn't know it would be this exhausting...

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:49.570
The more we try to keep up with Resistance Japan, the more we lose our stamina.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.360
It's not working out the way it always does...

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:54.150
They'll wear themselves out before we can destroy them.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.750
They're all a group of amateurs to begin with.

00:16:56.750 --> 00:16:59.280
None of them besides the Raimon trio can put up a decent fight.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:03.330
Coach Fudou is doing his job magnificently.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:07.540
You have yourself a wonderful ally.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.210
Your plays have gotten rather feeble.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:14.730
That's not true.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:19.600
You hurt your foot during your fight with Minamisawa-san.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.730
I just twisted it a little.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.330
It's not serious.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:25.940
Then what happened when Shindou-san gave you that pass?

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.300
You should have been able to receive it.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:29.440
What scared you?

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:31.540
Why did you run from the ball?

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.610
Me, run from the ball?

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:37.530
If you play like that, you'll get soccer taken from you as well.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:42.660
Soccer isn't as gentle as you seem to think.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:48.100
If you get intimidated and try to run, soccer will eat you up.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.400
What do you mean?

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.940
That's for you to find out.

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:57.190
Me...

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.170
Tsurugi.

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:02.350
I realized the meaning of this match.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:06.220
What they want to tell us through this game...

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:11.820
As Hakuryuu and the others shoot the ball towards us, the only answer we can give them in our current state is...

00:18:12.770 --> 00:18:13.230
Tenma!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.400
Show me the power of Inazuma Japan!

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:18.740
Tsurugi!

00:18:19.190 --> 00:18:21.950
Bicycle Sword!

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:31.860
Whoa!

00:18:32.680 --> 00:18:34.590
What an incredible clash of wills!

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:41.260
Why can't I steal it from him?

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.010
Was this all I could do?

00:18:46.170 --> 00:18:48.880
That can't be. We made it to the finals...

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.790
I ought to be able to do more...

00:18:52.410 --> 00:18:53.880
What's wrong with these guys?!

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:57.400
We're the representatives here! Let us win!

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.360
We can't be this bad.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:14.060
White Hurricane!

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:19.420
Wild Dun-

00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:38.030
How's your leg?

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:40.400
I'll manage.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.170
Soccer is a living thing.

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.910
It's a wild beast that will attack you if you look away from it.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.130
If you don't want to be swallowed up, don't look away.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:50.160
Keep your eyes on everything around you.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.770
Everything...

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:00.510
Hakuryuu.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.010
I guess I should say thank you.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:06.350
It was Coach Kuroiwa who ordered us to destroy you guys.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.920
It looks like that order was successfully executed.

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.680
It was worth our time coming here.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.690
Now you know the challenge you must face.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.860
Inazuma Japan.

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:22.820
You still have not made soccer your own.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:28.200
At the rate you're going, you couldn't possibly make even a dent against the strong opponents that are to come.

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:30.700
We've lost.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:36.900
But we will be sure to turn this defeat into something meaningful.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:39.550
Let's hope so.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:46.590
What was it that you wished for the team to be aware of?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:49.350
The terror of soccer.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.430
Terror?

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:57.440
This match was necessary if they are to continue winning.

00:20:57.970 --> 00:21:02.650
Soccer demands the furthest limits of power from those who face it.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:07.870
The closer you get to soccer, the greater becomes your risk at losing something that you once had.

00:21:08.550 --> 00:21:13.250
Let's take for instance Tetsukado Shin, whose door to his future closed because of his injury.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:18.500
Thus, you are saying that by understanding the terror of soccer, he will be able to conquer that terror...

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:23.310
But then, what lies ahead after they have conquered it?

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:24.470
The answer to that will come.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:30.100
And the moment they understand that, so will you.

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:44.940
Guys!

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:48.150
We can't just end today on a note like that.

00:21:48.150 --> 00:21:48.950
Yeah!

00:21:50.320 --> 00:21:51.970
A challenge, huh?

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:55.520
It's a big challenge for the three of us, too.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.250
It's time for the finals!

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:31.240
We'll change this overwhelming defeat into overwhelming strength!

00:23:31.240 --> 00:23:34.100
Next, Clash! Our Challenge To The World!!

00:23:34.310 --> 00:23:36.570
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:49.710
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:56.370
Soccer is a living thing. 
 It's a wild beast that will attack you if you look away from it!

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:57.370
That's all!
